.TH TEE 1 "2026" "spicule" "spicule User Commands"
.SH NAME
tee \- duplicate standard input
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tee
.RB [ \-ai ]
.RI [ file ]\ .\|.\|.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tee
copies standard input to standard output, making a copy in each
.I file
operand as well. Data is written out to standard output and to every
still-open destination file as soon as it is read, with no internal
buffering that would hold it back.
.PP
If a
.I file
operand cannot be opened, a diagnostic is written and that
destination is dropped before copying begins; the remaining
destinations, and standard output, still receive the full input. If a
write to an already-open destination fails partway through, a
diagnostic is written, that destination is closed and dropped, and
copying continues to the remaining destinations \(em a single broken
destination never stops the others, or standard output, from
receiving the rest of standard input.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-a
Append to each
.I file
operand instead of truncating it.
.TP
.B \-i
Ignore the
.B SIGINT
signal for the duration of the run.
.SH OPERANDS
.TP
.I file
A pathname of an output file. Unlike some operands elsewhere in this
suite,
.B \-
is not special here: a
.I file
operand of
.B \-
names a literal file called
.BR \- ,
not standard output.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Standard input was copied successfully to standard output and to
every
.I file
operand.
.TP
.B >0
An error occurred: an invalid option, a read error on standard input,
a write error on standard output, or a write error on one or more
.I file
operands (after any operands that failed to open at all were already
dropped).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cat (1)
